  "title": "Chapter cheat sheet — golden rules and traps",
  "board_content": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "text": "Fast-recall golden rules",
      "type": "heading",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "text": "Angles: any arc / sector / calculus formula assumes radians. Convert first, always.",
      "type": "note",
      "style": "red-margin",
      "emphasis": "high",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "text": "Functions: magnitude from the identity, sign from the quadrant — always two steps. Range-check every answer.",
      "type": "text",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 4,
      "text": "Allied angles: odd multiple of 90° ⇒ swap to co-function; sign from the quadrant via ASTC.",
      "type": "text",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 5,
      "text": "Graphs: divide (don't multiply) for the period; tangent's period is π; include the vertical shift in the range.",
      "type": "text",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 6,
      "text": "Identities: reconstruct everything from cos(A−B); watch every ±; amplitude is √(a²+b²), never a+b.",
      "type": "text",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 7,
      "text": "Equations: factor (never divide); back-check after squaring; keep the n; match the right solution family.",
      "type": "text",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    },
    {
      "seq": 8,
      "text": "If a final sin or cos exceeds 1 in magnitude, or a period looks multiplied not divided — stop and recheck.",
      "type": "note",
      "style": "red-margin",
      "emphasis": "normal",
      "reveal_at": 0
    }
  ],
